<urn:atm:triage:finding/ARCH-AI-001>
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-07-27T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:correctionNote "quality-mgr (2026-07-27): QA-1 for PR #667 (fix/phase-ai-arch-line-ceilings @ 46d2af22) closes this finding. crates/atm-daemon-client/src/lib.rs:20-23 now reads `pub use atm_core::doctor::{BootstrapAutoStartOutcome, BootstrapConnectOutcome, BootstrapLaunchGateOutcome, BootstrapTraceReport};` -- a re-export, not a redefinition. Sole canonical definition remains at crates/atm-core/src/doctor/report.rs:69-103. Workspace-wide grep sweep (ruthless-boundary-qa, req-qa, rust-qa-agent, rust-best-practices-agent, quality-mgr direct) confirms no other definition site exists anywhere in the workspace. Independently re-verified by 5 of 6 QA-1 reviewers plus quality-mgr direct source inspection; rust-qa-agent confirms fmt/clippy/tests all clean. New non-blocking follow-up: ruthless-boundary-qa found crates/atm/src/composition.rs:478 bootstrap_trace_to_core() is now a dead identity-conversion function (converts the type into itself via 15 redundant match arms, since this fix made atm_daemon_client's and atm_core's types identical via re-export) -- tracked as RBQA-F001, not blocking this closure." .